<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_WarLabContainmentCell - ANCIENT_WAR_LAB_1's core, the live-specimen
  half of the reveal-beat (with RUT_WarLabArchive carrying the records half).

  Item spec, criteria list: "Lab guardians read as mechanoid/ancient, never
  Assailant-flesh material (hard ban #8) ... live specimens exist only as
  sealed containment props/props-with-pawn, never a spawned hostile
  faction." the_propane_lakes.md's own reconciliation is explicit: "the
  study subjects here are live, trapped, and being studied ... not
  corpses" - so this cannot be flavor-text-only inert scenery pretending
  nothing is inside, but it ALSO must never risk spawning a hostile
  Assailant pawn on this map.

  DELIBERATE CHOICE, flagged rather than invented past: the criteria
  explicitly offers TWO satisfying shapes - "sealed containment props" OR
  "props-with-pawn". This file takes the props-only shape, not
  props-with-pawn, because props-with-pawn would need a confirmed
  Assailant PawnKindDef wired the way VAULT_DUNGEON_BUILD_1's
  RUT_Symbol_RakataCasket wraps AncientCryptosleepCasket with
  containPawnKindAnyOf - and that vanilla casket mechanism SPAWNS its
  contained pawn hostile the moment it is opened/breached
  (Building_AncientCryptosleepCasket's whole point). No Assailant
  PawnKindDef exists in this repo's authored content to check against
  (searched; none found), and inventing one now would be exactly the kind
  of content-palette invention ANCIENT_WAR_LAB_1.md's own "Watch out"
  section forbids for this pass ("do not invent — confirm at build time").
  A sealed, non-openable prop satisfies the ruled ban unambiguously; a
  live-pawn container version is real future work, once an Assailant
  study-subject PawnKindDef is confirmed and a non-breachable containment
  mechanic (or an explicit "opening this is a scripted quest event, not a
  free interaction") is designed - not guessed here.

  Not claimable, not deconstructible: a sealed system nobody on the crew
  understands well enough to strip for parts, matching the ban's own
  register (the study subject is dangerous if released, not a resource).

  Art: reuses Things/Building/Ship/ShipCryptosleepCasket (Core,
  Buildings_Misc.xml) at its native (1,2) proportions via drawSize only
  (footprint kept (1,1) so it never collides in a dense KCSG grid cell -
  the same size-vs-drawSize split RUT_VaultHeart/RUT_DarkTowerControlConsole
  already use for their own oversized single-cell props). Reading the shape
  of a sealed vertical pod without touching the vanilla ThingDef itself
  (Building_AncientCryptosleepCasket's className carries the openable/
  spawns-a-pawn behavior this file deliberately does not want) - no new art
  authored this pass.
-->
<Defs>
  <ThingDef ParentName="BuildingBase">
    <defName>RUT_WarLabContainmentCell</defName>
    <label>containment cell</label>
    <description>A sealed vertical tank, fogged with condensation on the inside of the glass. Something moves in there, unhurried, the way something moves when it has stopped trying to get out.\n\nNobody on the crew understands the seals well enough to trust them. Nobody is opening this.</description>
    <thingClass>Building</thingClass>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Building/Ship/ShipCryptosleepCasket</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>(1,2)</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <altitudeLayer>Building</altitudeLayer>
    <passability>Impassable</passability>
    <fillPercent>1</fillPercent>
    <rotatable>false</rotatable>
    <size>(1,1)</size>
    <tickerType>Never</tickerType>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>600</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
      <Beauty>-8</Beauty>
    </statBases>
    <building>
      <deconstructible>false</deconstructible>
      <claimable>false</claimable>
    </building>
  </ThingDef>
</Defs>
